<title>BRAZIL: Brazil to hold two June coffee sales.</title>
<headline>Brazil to hold two June coffee sales.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's government is to hold two auctions of its coffee stocks in June -- one of 150,000 bags on June 4 and a second sale of 42,250 bags on June 11, according to statements from Banco do Brasil.</p>
<p>Members of the domestic roasting and soluble coffee industry as well as exporters can participate in both auctions.</p>
<p>The Industry and Commerce Ministry decided to split its regular monthly sale of around 200,000 bags because of a food fair in Sao Paulo which is being held on June 10-13, said Mauricio Assis, head of the primary commodities department at the Industry and Commerce Ministry.</p>
<p>&quot;Normally with these kind of fairs there is a series of events. This (the June 11 auction) is a courtesy,&quot; Assis said.</p>
